{
  "$note": "HAND-WRITTEN. Each case patches conformance/validator-clean.json and states the diagnostics the semantic validator must produce, in order. `expect` entries are (rule, severity, path) triples: the message is deliberately NOT part of the cross-language contract, because it interpolates numbers and String(1.0) is '1' in JS while str(1.0) is '1.0' in Python. Every patched document is still SCHEMA-VALID -- that is the point: this file exercises the layer above the schema, and a mutation the schema already rejects belongs in the per-language bypass tests instead (see `unreachable_via_schema` below).",
  "clean": "validator-clean.json",
  "patch_ops": "Each op is {\"set\": path, \"value\": v} | {\"delete\": path} | {\"append\": path, \"value\": v}. `path` is slash-separated; a numeric segment indexes an array. Ops are applied in order to a deep copy of the clean document. A `value` that is a string beginning with \"@\" is a REFERENCE: the rest is a path read out of the UNMUTATED clean document, which is how a case names a generated block_id without hard-coding a digest that would rot the moment the identity formula moved.",
  "unreachable_via_schema": {
    "$note": "Rules that CANNOT fire on a schema-valid document, so they have no case here and are instead tested in each language by constructing the object behind the schema's back. This is a property of the rules, not a gap in the tests.",
    "G5": "Point/BBox are bounded to +/-20000 with allow_inf_nan false, so NaN/Infinity cannot survive Paper.model_validate or PaperSchema.parse.",
    "R30": "DESIGN.md 30 says so itself: the schema's if/then already requires model_id + prompt_hash and forces applied:false on ocr_correction / vlm_substitution. The rule is retained only for a better message.",
    "R30b-model-naming": "The mirror if/then forbids model_id / prompt_hash on deterministic kinds, so the 'a deterministic repair must not name a model' half of R30b is likewise schema-enforced. The from->to class check, which is NOT, is exercised by five cases below."
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "clean",
      "note": "the unmutated baseline: a semantically perfect document produces nothing at all",
      "ops": [],
      "expect": []
    },

    {
      "name": "R1-bbox-is-not-the-polygon-extent",
      "note": "widening bbox.x1 alone; the anchor (x0,y0) is untouched so the block id still checks out",
      "ops": [{ "set": "blocks/0/bbox/2", "value": 559 }],
      "expect": [{ "rule": "R1", "severity": "error", "path": "blocks[0].bbox" }]
    },
    {
      "name": "R2-span-bbox-is-inverted",
      "note": "x0 > x1 on a span box; block geometry is untouched so nothing else fires",
      "ops": [{ "set": "blocks/1/spans/0/bbox", "value": [292, 120, 54, 132] }],
      "expect": [{ "rule": "R2", "severity": "error", "path": "blocks[1].spans[0].bbox" }]
    },
    {
      "name": "R3-one-block-escapes-the-crop-box",
      "note": "a single marginally out-of-box block is parser jitter: WARN. The 5% threshold is raised so G7 does not promote it on a 5-block page.",
      "options": { "out_of_crop_box_error_fraction": 0.5 },
      "ops": [
        { "set": "blocks/4/polygon", "value": [[320, 308], [620, 308], [620, 332], [320, 332]] },
        { "set": "blocks/4/bbox", "value": [320, 308, 620, 332] }
      ],
      "expect": [{ "rule": "R3", "severity": "warning", "path": "blocks[4].polygon" }]
    },
    {
      "name": "G7-a-systematic-coordinate-space-error",
      "note": "2 of 5 blocks on page 0 leave the crop box: 40% is not jitter, so rule 3 is promoted to ERROR and reported as G7",
      "ops": [
        { "set": "blocks/3/polygon", "value": [[320, 120], [620, 120], [620, 300], [320, 300]] },
        { "set": "blocks/3/bbox", "value": [320, 120, 620, 300] },
        { "set": "blocks/4/polygon", "value": [[320, 308], [620, 308], [620, 332], [320, 332]] },
        { "set": "blocks/4/bbox", "value": [320, 308, 620, 332] }
      ],
      "expect": [
        { "rule": "G7", "severity": "error", "path": "blocks[3].polygon" },
        { "rule": "G7", "severity": "error", "path": "blocks[4].polygon" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "G4-page-width-disagrees-with-crop-box",
      "ops": [{ "set": "pages/0/width", "value": 600 }],
      "expect": [{ "rule": "G4", "severity": "error", "path": "pages[0].width" }]
    },
    {
      "name": "G4-crop-box-does-not-start-at-the-origin",
      "note": "width and height still agree with the box, so only the D23 origin clause fires",
      "ops": [{ "set": "pages/0/crop_box", "value": [10, 10, 622, 802] }],
      "expect": [{ "rule": "G4", "severity": "error", "path": "pages[0].crop_box" }]
    },
    {
      "name": "G6-degenerate-polygon",
      "note": "three collinear vertices: zero area, and the bowtie half is deliberately not also reported",
      "ops": [
        { "set": "blocks/4/polygon", "value": [[320, 308], [440, 308], [558, 308]] },
        { "set": "blocks/4/bbox", "value": [320, 308, 558, 308] }
      ],
      "expect": [{ "rule": "G6", "severity": "error", "path": "blocks[4].polygon" }]
    },
    {
      "name": "G6-self-intersecting-ring",
      "note": "area 3336 pt2 and the same extent, so only the bowtie clause fires - a parser bug, hence WARN",
      "ops": [
        {
          "set": "blocks/4/polygon",
          "value": [[320, 308], [558, 320], [400, 308], [558, 332], [320, 332]]
        }
      ],
      "expect": [{ "rule": "G6", "severity": "warning", "path": "blocks[4].polygon" }]
    },
    {
      "name": "G8-geometry-at-the-wrong-scale-for-its-page",
      "note": "page 1 blown up to 20000x20000 with a matching crop box: G4 and rule 3 both still pass, and only G8 notices that the blocks now cover 0.001% of it. This is the same detection as geometry stored in normalised [0,1] fractions, from the other side. G8 is a WARNING (DESIGN.md 5.2): low coverage is suspicion, not proof the document is wrong.",
      "ops": [
        { "set": "pages/1/width", "value": 20000 },
        { "set": "pages/1/height", "value": 20000 },
        { "set": "pages/1/crop_box", "value": [0, 0, 20000, 20000] },
        { "set": "pages/1/media_box", "value": [0, 0, 20000, 20000] }
      ],
      "expect": [{ "rule": "G8", "severity": "warning", "path": "pages[1]" }]
    },

